> Retain the original seeded edge/noise experiment

The native fixture creates the original40-by40 image: columns0..19 contain60 and
columns20..39 contain200. In row-major order, mt19937_64 seed7 supplies a
uniform draw; draws below0.15 trigger a second draw selecting zero or255 at
threshold0.5. We retain every original draw and branch, then call the same
radius-one native producer. The standard library’s distribution sequence is
reproduced for this build, without a cross-vendor bitstream promise.

The figure uses the same grayscale range0..255 in every panel. Image rows
increase upwards in this coordinate display; row0 is the bottom row.
Clean/noisy/filtered panels show actual integer images, with no independent
image-processing implementation in the report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/median_filter_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/median_filter.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto d = dm::algorithms::median_filter_demo();
    std::print("| actual candidate | pixels | changed from clean | exact zero or255 | mean absolute error | " "maximum absolute error |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto pair : {std::pair{"noisy", d.noisy_summary},
                      std::pair{"filtered", d.filtered_summary}}) {
        auto &s = pair.second;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.8f} | {} |\n", pair.first,
                   s.pixels, s.changed, s.extremes, s.mean_absolute_error,
                   s.maximum_absolute_error);
    }
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 2);
    std::vector<double> axis(40);
    std::iota(axis.begin(), axis.end(), 0.);
    std::size_t index = 0;
    for (auto &image : std::vector<std::vector<std::vector<int>> >{
         d.clean, d.noisy, d.filtered.image
     }) {
        std::vector<std::vector<double>> z(40, std::vector<double>(40));
        for (std::size_t row = 0; row < 40; ++row)
            for (std::size_t col = 0; col < 40; ++col)
                z[col][row] = image[row][col];
        auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
        p.image(axis, axis, z,
                {{0, 0, 0}, {64, 64, 64}, {128, 128, 128}, {192, 192, 192},
                 {255, 255, 255}}, 0, 255).x_limits(-.5, 39.5).y_limits(-.5,
                                                                        39.5).x_label("input column").y_label("input row, increasing up").margins(80, 30, 50, 60).title(std::vector<std::string>{"Actual clean step", "Actual seed7 noisy image", "Actual radius-one median"}[index++]);
        layout.add(p);
    }
    layout.size(1100, 1100).fit_panels().save_svg("build/median_filter_original.svg");
}
```
