> Extreme counts do not capture every error

A residual pixel need not be zero or255 to differ from clean data. A majority of
neighbouring200 values can replace a clean60, and neither value counts as an
extreme. The next figure therefore shows both exact0/255 counts and all changed
pixels against the known clean reference. These are measurements on this one
seeded image, not a guaranteed improvement for all inputs or a noise-model
inference.

The local median is insensitive to outlier magnitude when fewer than half of the
window samples are corrupted in a constant region. Mixed clean regions have
their own rank structure; boundary replication, high local corruption and narrow
features can change the result. The loss function proof is local and should not
be confused with a global reconstruction guarantee.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/median_filter_errors.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/median_filter.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto d = dm::algorithms::median_filter_demo();
    std::print("| actual observation | value |\n| --- | ---: |\n| accepted corruption draws | {} |\n| noisy " "changed pixels | {} |\n| filtered changed pixels | {} |\n| noisy exact extremes | {} |\n| " "filtered exact extremes | {} |\n| actual filtered left probe | {} |\n| actual filtered " "right probe | {} |\n",
               d.corruptions, d.noisy_summary.changed,
               d.filtered_summary.changed, d.noisy_summary.extremes,
               d.filtered_summary.extremes, d.filtered.image[20][5],
               d.filtered.image[20][35]);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(d.noisy_summary.changed),
                                      double(d.filtered_summary.changed),
                                      double(d.noisy_summary.extremes),
                                      double(d.filtered_summary.extremes)},
                                     {"noisy errors", "filtered errors",
                                      "noisy extremes", "filtered extremes"},
                                     "actual pixels");
    p.x_label("actual clean-reference or extreme criterion").y_label(
        "actual pixel count").title("Original seed7: all errors and extremes are distinct").save_svg("build/median_filter_errors.svg");
}
