| prescribed clean fixture | actual changed pixels | actual samples | actual output pixels |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| broad aligned step | 0 | 225 | 25 |
| single column stripe | 5 | 225 | 25 |
\image(figures/median_filter_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual change counts on two clean structures.)
\alttext(The broad aligned step is preserved; all five stripe pixels disappear.)

> Verification and references

Native tests enumerate all512 binary3-square images at radii0,1,2 and compare
with independently fully sorted clamped windows. They inspect every actual
sample address/value, completed output span/median, work count and quota. The
original40-square seeded image and filter are checked against the original draw
order and independent sorting. Tests distinguish thin-feature loss from a
preserved broad step, and cover identity/empty shapes, complete malformed-input
guards, exact capture admission, ownership and full-int-range difference
summaries. Existing image regressions remain. The shared ten-report batch passes
71 CTest cases, 29 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 130 compiled and
executed public examples, 598/598 scoped documentation definitions and ten
representative hovers. Independent Python arbitrary-precision, hashlib,
sorted-window, RNG, polynomial, graph and full-assignment references verify
224,229 actual records. Frozen comparisons preserve ordinary legacy outputs,
including selected clique identities, original density graphs and memetic
partitions. Twelve checkout headers and twelve identically installed headers
compile independently; an installed-header native consumer links and runs. All
four complete programs and all four native figures pass execution and visual
review, and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed results and identical image
bytes. Receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-224-233/`.

Median smoothing is a standard nonlinear order-statistic method; see Tukey,
*Exploratory Data Analysis* (1977). The local absolute-deviation
characterization and replicated-border semantics used here are derived
explicitly above. The report makes no universal restoration or edge-preservation
claim.
